# Tortoise blog admin SPA — environment
# Copy to .env for local dev. Same Supabase project as the site
# (the blog_posts / blog_admins tables + blog-images bucket live there).

# Supabase project (see website/functions/blog/_lib.ts for the project ref)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://ybetwichurajbfswfeqa.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste-the-project-anon-key-here

# The SPA's DIRECT Supabase calls authenticate with the legacy
# `sb-tortoise-auth-token` parent-domain cookie (`src/lib/supabase.ts`) — issued
# by the MCP consent page in `tortoise/oauth.py`, and re-written on refresh by
# this app's own `writeCookie` (`src/lib/supabase.ts`) — NOT by the BFF. That is a
# retained legacy credential to be migrated onto the BFF (#4178); the session
# gate itself is the HttpOnly `__Host-session`, read via `/api/session`.
# No service-role keys client-side.
